.\" Process this file with
.\" groff -man -Tascii rmdir.2
.\"
.TH RMDIR 2 "2026-02-28" "Substrate Kernel" "System Calls Manual"
.SH NAME
rmdir \- delete a directory
.SH LIBRARY
Standard C library (libc, -lc)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <unistd.h>
.PP
.BI "int rmdir(const char *" pathname ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rmdir()
deletes a directory, which must be empty.
.SH RETURN VALUE
On success, zero is returned. On error, -1 is returned.
.SH ERRORS
.TP
.B EACCES
Write or search permission denied for the directory containing
.IR pathname .
.TP
.B EROFS
.I pathname
is on a read-only mount.
.TP
.B EPERM
The directory containing
.I pathname
has the sticky bit set, and the caller owns neither it nor the
directory being removed (and is not the superuser).
.TP
.B ENOTEMPTY
The directory is not empty.
.TP
.B ENOENT
The directory does not exist.

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR intro(2)
